  "system": {
    "finalName": "",
    "description": "<p><i>Reference Book:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars_Saga_Edition_Unknown_Regions\" title=\"Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions\">Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions</a></i> </p><p>The projectile equivalent of a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Heavy_Blaster_Pistol\" title=\"Heavy Blaster Pistol\">Heavy Blaster Pistol</a>, the Heavy Slugthrower Pistol uses a larger round than a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Slugthrower_Pistol\" title=\"Slugthrower Pistol\">Slugthrower Pistol</a>, creating greater stopping power at the cost of increased recoil, which makes accurate firing of several shots in rapid succession a difficult prospect. </p><p>In spite of this lack of accuracy, the Heavy Slugthrower Pistol does provide a psychological advantage, both because of its large size as well as the loud report it makes when fired, something to be considered when dealing with a skittish group of unfriendly natives. </p><p>If you use the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Double_Attack\" title=\"Double Attack\">Double Attack</a>, <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Triple_Attack\" title=\"Triple Attack\">Triple Attack</a>, or <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Rapid_Shot\" title=\"Rapid Shot\">Rapid Shot</a> feats with a Heavy Slugthrower Pistol, you take an additional -1 penalty to attack rolls. A Heavy Slugthrower Pistol uses an ammo clip instead of a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Power_Pack\" title=\"Power Pack\">Power Pack</a>. After 8 shots, the clip must be replaced. A clip costs 15 credits and weighs 0.1 kg. </p>",
